cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit or cite the findings, please cite as below."
title: >-
  Erasures, not errors: machine-checked arithmetic and the correction
  record of the Linear A accounting tablets (research report and toolkit)
authors:
  - family-names: Gurdzhi
    given-names: Dmitry Felix
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2718-9682"
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/deemkeen/linear-a-arithmetic"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Linear A
  - Minoan Crete
  - epigraphy
  - computational philology
  - Haghia Triada
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked arithmetic, hypothesis testing, and apparatus mining
  over the Linear A corpus. Arithmetic discrepancies on the Haghia
  Triada tablets correlate with erasures in numeral lines (p = 0.003):
  the "calculation errors" of Linear A are residues of document
  updates, not scribal incompetence. Includes column constraints on
  the disputed fraction values and six pre-registered predictions.
